# 0335 — register the PANDORA / Popsicle drivers in bsd/conf/files.
#
# RECORD ONLY. This patch is what the registration looks like, not the way to
# apply it. A static patch cannot ask "is this line already there", so a second
# `git apply` of this file fails with:
#
#   error: patch failed: bsd/conf/files:134
#   error: bsd/conf/files: patch does not apply
#
# The idempotent mechanism is tools/register-drivers.sh, which checks before it
# appends and can be re-run at any time:
#
#   tools/register-drivers.sh /opt/work/ci/buildtree/xnu
#
# It registers the same fourteen sources below and additionally wires four init
# calls into the sweet_ufs.c bring-up block (bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c is not in this
# repository, so that half of the work cannot live in a patch against it):
# redwood_input_init(), pandora_sensors_init(), pandora_idle_init() and
# pandora_mem_init(). This file is kept so the conf/files change is reviewable in
# the same diff form as 0333 and 0334.
#
# bsd/dev/pandora_touch.c is NOT in this hunk: it sits at line 112 of the
# upstream file, above bsd/dev/pandora_amp.c, and was already registered there.
# The script only verifies that line still exists and never moves it.
#
# Header files are not listed in conf/files — the file has no .h entry at all.
# bsd/sys/redwood_input.h is found through the include path; it ships in 0334.
#
--- a/bsd/conf/files
+++ b/bsd/conf/files
@@ -134,6 +134,20 @@
 bsd/dev/pandora_cpu.c			standard
 bsd/dev/pandora_autoswipe.c		standard
 bsd/dev/pandora_dpu.c			standard
+bsd/dev/pandora_bt.c		standard
+bsd/dev/pandora_modem.c		standard
+bsd/dev/pandora_thermal.c	standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_wifi.c		standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_audio.c	standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_camera.c	standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_fp.c		standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_modem.c	standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_syna.c		standard
+bsd/dev/popsicle_goodix.c	standard
+bsd/dev/redwood_input.c		standard
+bsd/dev/pandora_sensors.c	standard
+bsd/dev/pandora_idle.c		standard
+bsd/dev/pandora_mem.c		standard
 bsd/dev/adreno/ArmSmmu4K.c		standard
 bsd/dev/adreno/ArmSmmu4KContext.c	standard
 bsd/dev/adreno/ArmSmmu4KProgram.c	standard
